---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const title = 'Terms & Conditions | Amido';
const description = 'The terms that apply to the Amido website, applications and subscriptions.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="py-16 md:py-24 bg-white">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6">
      <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <header class="mb-10">
          <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 mb-4 tracking-tight">Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-600">
            These terms govern your use of the Amido website and applications.
          </p>
        </header>

        <section class="space-y-4 mb-10">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">1. Who we are and acceptance</h2>
          <p>Amido is provided by <strong class="text-gray-900">Emanuele Viglianisi</strong>, Altenbauerstraße 12, 4060 Leonding, Austria (“we”, “us”). By using the Amido website or applications, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please do not use Amido.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4 mb-10">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">2. What Amido is — and is not</h2>
          <p>Amido is an informational food logger. It helps you record meals and estimate ingredients, quantities, calories, macronutrients, fiber and glycemic impact from text, photos or barcodes, and it can log meals to your own Nightscout.</p>
          <p>Amido is <strong class="text-gray-900">not a medical device</strong> and does not provide medical, nutritional or therapeutic advice, diagnosis or treatment. Estimates come from automated systems and public databases and may be inaccurate, incomplete or unsuitable for your situation. You are responsible for independently verifying all information against product labels or other authoritative sources, in particular before using it for carbohydrate counting, insulin dosing or any dietary or medical decision.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4 mb-10">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">3. Your account</h2>
          <p>To use Amido you need an account and sign in with Google or Apple. You are responsible for the accuracy of the information you provide, for keeping access to your sign-in provider account secure, and for all activity under your account. Your diary is stored on your device and is not synced across devices; use the export feature if you want a backup. You must be old enough to enter into a binding agreement in your jurisdiction and, where required, have the consent of a parent or guardian.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4 mb-10">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">4. Acceptable use</h2>
          <p>You agree not to misuse Amido. In particular, you must not attempt to disrupt or overload the service or its AI providers, access it using automated means beyond normal use, reverse-engineer or circumvent usage limits, upload unlawful content, or use Amido in a way that infringes the rights of others or violates applicable law.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4 mb-10">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">5. Content you submit</h2>
          <p>You keep ownership of the meal descriptions, photos and other content you submit. You grant us a limited licence to process that content solely to operate the service — for example, to send it to an AI provider for analysis. The resulting diary entry is stored on your device, not on our servers. You confirm that you have the right to submit the content and that it does not infringe third-party rights.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4 mb-10">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">6. Subscriptions and payments</h2>
          <p>Amido is offered as a paid subscription. Payments are handled by the Apple App Store or Google Play in the mobile apps, or by Stripe on the web, each under its own terms. Prices, billing period, renewal and cancellation are shown at the point of purchase. Unless stated otherwise, subscriptions renew automatically and can be cancelled through the provider you purchased from.</p>
          <p>If you are a consumer in the European Union, you generally have a right of withdrawal for distance contracts. Where a subscription provides immediate access to digital content or services, you may be asked to consent to immediate performance and acknowledge that you lose the withdrawal right once performance has begun. Statutory rights, including rights in respect of defective content, remain unaffected.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4 mb-10">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">7. Availability, changes and termination</h2>
          <p>Amido is provided on an “as available” basis. We may add, change, suspend or discontinue features, and may impose fair-use limits, at any time. We may suspend or terminate access if these terms are breached. You may stop using Amido at any time, delete the diary from your device in Settings → Your data, and delete your account, which removes the account, usage counters and subscription data from our servers.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4 mb-10">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">8. Intellectual property</h2>
          <p>The Amido name, logo, interface and software are protected by intellectual-property laws. These terms do not grant you any right to use them except as needed to use the service. Public food data used by Amido remains subject to the terms of its providers (for example, Open Food Facts data is available under the ODbL).</p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4 mb-10">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">9. Disclaimers and limitation of liability</h2>
          <p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, Amido is provided without warranties of any kind, including accuracy, completeness or fitness for a particular purpose. We do not warrant that estimates are correct or that the service will be uninterrupted or error-free.</p>
          <p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, we are not liable for indirect or consequential damages, or for any decision or action taken in reliance on Amido's estimates. Nothing in these terms limits liability where it cannot be limited by law, including liability for intent or gross negligence, or for death or personal injury caused by our fault. Mandatory consumer rights remain unaffected.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4 mb-10">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">10. Governing law and contact</h2>
          <p>These terms are governed by Austrian law, without prejudice to the mandatory consumer-protection rules of your country of residence. Questions about these terms can be sent to <a href="mailto:emavgl.app@gmail.com" class="text-brand hover:underline">emavgl.app@gmail.com</a>.</p>
        </section>

        <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 border-t border-gray-200 pt-6">Last updated: 26 October 2026</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
